--------------------------------------------------------------------------
How JUCE constrains this choice
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHRONA is built with the JUCE framework (https://juce.com). JUCE is dual
licensed. Your distribution license MUST be consistent with the JUCE license
you build under:

  • JUCE under GPLv3  → the binary you ship must also be GPLv3 (you may sell
    it, but you must offer the corresponding source). If you go this route,
    replace this file with the standard GPLv3 text (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt)
    and keep JUCE_DISPLAY_SPLASH_SCREEN as required by that license tier.

  • JUCE commercial license (Indie / Pro / paid)  → you may ship CHRONA as a
    closed-source proprietary product under your own EULA. If you go this
    route, replace this file with your proprietary EULA (a starting template
    is in EULA.txt) and keep proof of your JUCE license.

Until you pick one, do NOT publish a public binary: shipping a splash-free,
closed build without a paid JUCE license violates the JUCE GPL terms.

